<concept id="t00757">
	<title>Jack label</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>jack label</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<fig id="e04616">
			<title>Type A</title>
			<image href="images/OMQ4A065015.jpg" scale="70" align="center" placement="break"/>
		</fig>
		<fig id="e04617">
			<title>Type B</title>
			<image href="images/OMQ4A065016.jpg" scale="70" align="center" placement="break"/>
		</fig>
		<fig id="e04618">
			<title>Type C</title>
			<image href="images/OMQ4A065017.jpg" scale="70" align="center" placement="break"/>
		</fig>
		<fig id="e04619"><?oxy_comment_start author="june" timestamp="20250825T153208+0900" comment="호주 ONLY"?>
			<title>Type D</title><?oxy_comment_end?>
			<image href="images/N_TK25F027_E.jpg" scale="70" align="center" placement="break"/>
		</fig>
		<p>The actual jack label in your vehicle may differ from the illustration above. Refer to the jack label in your vehicle for these specifications:</p>
		<ol outputclass="callout" id="e04620">
			<li>
				<p>Model Name</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Maximum allowable load</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>When using the jack, apply your parking brake</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>When using the jack, stop the engine</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Do not get under a vehicle that is supported by a jack</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Use the designated jack locations under the frame</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>When supporting the vehicle, the base plate of the jack must be vertical under the lifting point</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Shift to P (Park) <?oxy_comment_start author="june" timestamp="20250825T153041+0900" comment="MT ONLY"?> or R (Reverse) for Manual Transmission <?oxy_comment_end?></p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>The jack should be used on firm, level ground</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Jack manufacturer</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Production date</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Representative company and address</p>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</conbody>
